  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nAnecdotally, I often come across situations where authors want to use a `legend`, but due to the layout/styling they're trying to implement they need to have additional `div` or `span` elements around the legend - breaking the legend in the process (and then not realising until somebody tests their form with a screen reader).\n\nI'm wondering if there's any chance of relaxing/removing the requirement for `legend` to be the first child of a `fieldset` https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-legend-element\n\nApart from needing to change the \"plumbing\" in browsers to still recognise and expose the content of the legend even when it's not the first child, would this cause any other unforeseen problems? Ambiguity about \"what happens then if there's more than one `legend`? (which could be resolved perhaps by saying that the first `legend` encountered when going through the child elements/tree/hierarchy of the `fieldset` is the one that then \"sticks\")\n\nx-ref https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6645",
